WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.335
-Hello, everyone,
and welcome back to the attic.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.503
Last week, my dog Frisbee sat

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.504
in that tiny chair back there.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:05.672
Many of you Instagrammed it,

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.807
justifying an otherwise
pointless purchase

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:09.275
of a chair too small
for an adult

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.476
and too boring for a child.

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:12.678
Well, now that the chair's
been used on TV,

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:13.880
my accountant informs me

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.415
that it is a tax write-off,
which is great.

00:00:16.415 --> 00:00:18.517
Unfortunately,
my accountant is also a wasp,

00:00:18.517 --> 00:00:20.853
so I'm not sure how much
he knows about human finance.

00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:23.122
He spent most of his time
at the accounting firm

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:25.024
Ernst &amp; Stung.

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:26.025
[ Laughs ] And you can tell
he's an accountant

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:27.026
because he wrote that joke.

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:28.528
And, speaking of jokes --
[ Ding ]

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.196
The president
is reeling politically

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:32.932
from his deadly incompetence
during the coronavirus pandemic

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:35.267
and, now, he and his
sycophants on state TV

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:38.237
are trying to distract from that
by obsessively spinning

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:40.606
wild conspiracy theories
about Barack Obama.

00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:43.543
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:47.513
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]

00:00:47.513 --> 00:00:50.249
Well, it's just another day
in the rolling nightmare

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:51.517
that is the Trump era.

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:54.120
I wish I could just walk
outta his presidency

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.622
the way he walked out of that
press conference on Monday

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:58.324
when reporters dared to ask him

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.126
even mildly
challenging questions.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.994
-Okay, anybody else?

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:03.596
Please, go ahead.
In the back, please.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.398
-I have two questions.
-No, it's okay.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.765
We'll go over here.
-But you pointed to me.

00:01:06.765 --> 00:01:07.800
I have two questions,

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.368
Mr. President.
-Next. Next, please.

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:11.437
-But you called on me.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:14.707
-I did, and you didn't respond
and, now, I'm calling on

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:15.941
-Sorry. I just wanted to let --
-the young lady in the back.

00:01:15.941 --> 00:01:17.043
Please.
-I just wanted to let

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:18.344
my colleague finish. But can I
-Okay.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.378
-ask you a question, please?
-Ladies and gentlemen,

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:20.846
thank you very much.
Appreciate it.

00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:22.015
-But you called on me.
-Thank you very much.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:24.583
-You called on me.

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:26.052
-You know,
it's a lot less dramatic

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:28.054
when you try to storm out
of your own press conference

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.522
and in front of the cameras,
no less.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.991
It's like trying to walk
out of a meeting on Zoom

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.459
and forgetting
where your door is.

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:34.860
"Alright, you know what?

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.762
This is ridiculous.
I quit!

00:01:36.762 --> 00:01:39.031
Goodbye, everybody!

00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:40.900
Goodbye!

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.302
Had it with you.

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.674
Also, could you guys log out?
I need this Zoom room

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:50.309
for my dog's birthday party
in like 10 minutes.

00:01:50.309 --> 00:01:52.077
Yeah, I don't wear pants!

00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:54.213
Not shoes, but pants.

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:56.849
Also, dude,
you can't just walk out.

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:58.951
You left all your props
on the table.

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:01.087
-This major commitment
is possible

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:03.089
because of the
massive mobilization

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:06.425
of American industry, including
Puritan Medical Products,

00:02:06.425 --> 00:02:09.929
U.S. Cotton, Abbott Labs,
and Thermo Fisher.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.664
Some of these
incredible companies

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:14.833
produce and produced
rapidly for us

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:17.837
and their products are here
with us this afternoon.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.172
These are all different products

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:22.374
that were literally
just developed,

00:02:22.374 --> 00:02:25.211
if you can imagine that,
and these are the best machines

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.846
and the best equipment
anywhere in the world.

00:02:27.846 --> 00:02:29.381
-Yo, cool.
It's like QVC,

00:02:29.381 --> 00:02:31.917
if the "C" stood
for coronavirus.

00:02:31.917 --> 00:02:34.254
Where have I seen Trump
pull that move before?

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:35.254
-There's the water company.

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:36.623
I mean, we sell water.

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:37.856
Trump Steaks.
Where are the steaks?

00:02:37.856 --> 00:02:39.058
Do we have steaks?
Right.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:41.026
[ Cheering and applause ]
We have Trump Steaks.

00:02:41.026 --> 00:02:43.429
And, by the way,
if you wanna take one,

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:44.597
we'll charge you about, what?

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:45.664
Fifty bucks a steak.

00:02:45.664 --> 00:02:46.865
[ Laughter ]
No, I won't.

00:02:46.865 --> 00:02:47.866
The magazine is great.

00:02:47.866 --> 00:02:49.368
Anybody want one?
Here, take one.

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:51.804
And, by the way, the winery --
you see the wine --

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.473
we make the finest wine,
as good a wine

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:55.474
as you can get
anywhere in the world

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:57.643
and I know the press
is extremely honest,

00:02:57.643 --> 00:02:59.179
so I won't offer them any,
but, if they want,

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:00.946
they can take a bottle
of wine home.

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:03.183
-His timing on the free wine
was four years too early.

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:04.250
He could be rakin' it
in right now.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.319
Also, wine?
You should be handin' out

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:07.886
tequila shots
at your press conference.

00:03:07.886 --> 00:03:09.155
[ As Trump ]
Everyone get blackout drunk

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:12.391
'cause I'd love if we all
forgot this ever happened.

00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:14.593
The president pulled the same
move for coronavirus tests

00:03:14.593 --> 00:03:16.929
that he previously used
for his crappy steaks and wine.

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:18.330
If the pattern holds,
we'll be back here

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.399
in four years
with Trump selling steaks,

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:22.201
nose swabs,
and zombie repellant.

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:25.371
Living through this presidency
means living in a constant state

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.806
of being both shocked and numb
at the same time.

00:03:27.806 --> 00:03:30.042
In fact, that's what
they're counting on.

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:32.744
One advisor to the White House
Coronavirus Task Force

00:03:32.744 --> 00:03:34.146
told The Washington Post,

00:03:34.146 --> 00:03:37.483
"The question is will people
become anesthetized to it?"

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.785
Well, I'm pretty sure Trump

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:40.419
has been anesthetized
since day one.

00:03:40.419 --> 00:03:42.988
His presidency has been
like one long YouTube video

00:03:42.988 --> 00:03:45.390
of a kid comin' home
from the dentist.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.493
[ As Trump ]
Is this real life?

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.497
And Trump's face
is always frozen

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:52.998
in that dead-eyed grimace,

00:03:52.998 --> 00:03:55.300
like he wears a night cream
made of Novocaine,

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.436
which, incidentally,
you can find on the Goop store,

00:03:57.436 --> 00:03:59.471
under Moon Powders.

00:03:59.471 --> 00:04:00.639
Of course, the reality is

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:02.141
Americans are not
anesthetized to it.

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:04.010
The vast majority of Americans

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.713
overwhelmingly support
social distancing measures

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:08.681
and say public health
is more important

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:10.483
than prematurely reopening
the economy.

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.485
And, in a new poll
out yesterday,

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.887
54% of Americans continue to say

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.655
the U.S. government
is doing a poor job

00:04:16.655 --> 00:04:18.658
preventing the spread
of COVID-19

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:20.959
and only 36% say
they consider Trump

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:23.228
a trusted source of information
about the outbreak.

00:04:23.228 --> 00:04:25.364
Wow!
That is shocking.

00:04:25.364 --> 00:04:27.266
I mean, how could you not
trust the guy who said

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:28.567
heat would kill
the coronavirus,

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:29.935
that cases would go
down to zero,

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:31.003
that it would go away in April,

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:32.504
that a vaccine
would come out soon,

00:04:32.504 --> 00:04:34.774
that hydroxychloroquine
could be a gift from heaven,

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.675
and that it could be cured
by eating Lysol wipes

00:04:36.675 --> 00:04:38.777
out of a salad bowl
with a fork and a knife?

00:04:38.777 --> 00:04:40.146
[ As Trump ]
And, for a little flavor,

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:42.982
throw in some croutons
and some balsamic disinfectant.

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.817
And, if you compare
Trump's approval rating

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.119
to governors and foreign leaders

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:47.519
who've handled
the outbreak competently,

00:04:47.519 --> 00:04:48.554
they look even worse,

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:50.322
like New Zealand's
prime minister,

00:04:50.322 --> 00:04:52.725
Jacinda Ardern,
who's handling has won more

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:55.061
than 80% public approval,
well above any leader

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:57.196
in the Group of Seven
wealthy democracies.

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:58.764
Or the popularity of governors

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:00.867
who have responded much more
aggressively to the crisis

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:02.100
on both sides of the aisle.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.470
-In Massachusetts,
84% approve

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.372
of how Republican
Governor Charlie Baker

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.274
has handled
the coronavirus outbreak,

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:10.610
according to a new poll
out this week.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.712
California's Democratic
governor, Gavin Newsom,

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:15.814
hit 83% approval of his
performance last month,

00:05:15.814 --> 00:05:18.584
nearly double his
pre-coronavirus numbers.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:21.120
Jay Inslee, in Washington,
is also way up.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:25.124
He received a 75% positive
approval rating in another poll.

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:26.358
-83%!

00:05:26.358 --> 00:05:28.795
Do you know what
Donald Trump would do

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:30.562
for an 83% approval rating?

00:05:30.562 --> 00:05:34.533
I don't think he's that high
among Trump's ages 30 to 60.

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:36.402
And Trump is clearly aware
that governors

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:37.803
are much more popular
than he is

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:41.173
because he sees their numbers
and wants credit for them.

00:05:41.173 --> 00:05:42.741
On Tuesday, he tweeted,

00:05:42.741 --> 00:05:45.144
"Remember this, every Governor
who has sky high approval

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:46.612
on their handling
of the Coronavirus,

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:48.881
and I am happy for them all,
could in no way

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:50.716
have gotten those numbers,
or had that success,

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:52.384
without me and the
Federal Governments help.

00:05:52.384 --> 00:05:55.621
From Ventilators to Testing,
we made it happen!

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:57.356
Also, Hillary only won
the popular vote

00:05:57.356 --> 00:05:59.158
because people hated me,
so you're welcome."

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:00.859
And, no, you didn't
make it happen.

00:06:00.859 --> 00:06:03.529
You can't tell states to get
lost when they want help,

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:05.331
then claim credit
when they succeed.

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:08.367
This isn't Don Jr.'s
sixth grade science project.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.036
[ As Trump ]
Idiot. You're not supposed
to pour baking soda

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.503
